{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778977612870,"sessionID":"ses_1ccabf5d9ffeZtpHMjPNmVB0Gb","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_CznqKBxu7xhZ5clgAD6DISfR","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/__issue_context__.json","offset":1,"limit":400},"output":"<path>/__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/__issue_context__.json</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: {\n2:   \"body\": \"**Preferred gene-related syndrome label**\\nGPR161-related medulloblastoma predisposition\\n\\n**Synonyms**\\n\\n**Parent term (use [OLS](https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols/ontologies/mondo), or your favorite ontology browser)**\\n\\n**Definition**\\nA predisposition to medulloblastoma, a tumor that originates in the cerebellum and dorsal brainstem, has a peak incidence in childhood, and makes up a large proportion of embryonal brain tumors. \\n\\n\\n**Definition source (Please give PubMed ID, if applicable, in format PMID:#######)\\n\\n**Children terms (if applicable)** Should any existing terms be re-classified as children underneath this new proposed term? \\n\\n**Your nano-attribution (ORCID) or URL for a working group**\\nhttps://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/\\n\\nThis is a priority disease name for ClinGen. If this request could please be processed as soon as possible, it would be greatly appreciated!\\n\\n\",\n3:   \"comments\": [],\n4:   \"title\": \"GPR161-related medulloblastoma predisposition\",\n5:   \"url\": \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9877\"\n6: }\n\n(End of file - total 6 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"{\n  \"body\": \"**Preferred gene-related syndrome label**\\nGPR161-related medulloblastoma predisposition\\n\\n**Synonyms**\\n\\n**Parent term (use [OLS](https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols/ontologies/mondo), or your favorite ontology browser)**\\n\\n**Definition**\\nA predisposition to medulloblastoma, a tumor that originates in the cerebellum and dorsal brainstem, has a peak incidence in childhood, and makes up a large proportion of embryonal brain tumors. \\n\\n\\n**Definition source (Please give PubMed ID, if applicable, in format PMID:#######)\\n\\n**Children terms (if applicable)** Should any existing terms be re-classified as children underneath this new proposed term? \\n\\n**Your nano-attribution (ORCID) or URL for a working group**\\nhttps://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/\\n\\nThis is a priority disease name for ClinGen. If this request could please be processed as soon as possible, it would be greatly appreciated!\\n\\n\",\n  \"comments\": [],\n  \"title\": \"GPR161-related medulloblastoma predisposition\",\n  \"url\": \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9877\"\n}","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"__issue_context__.json","time":{"start":1778977612852,"end":1778977612868}},"id":"prt_e33542429001svsViKwIeG5av6","sessionID":"ses_1ccabf5d9ffeZtpHMjPNmVB0Gb","messageID":"msg_e33540b3f001ZbrpR16psUp6lD"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778977612912,"sessionID":"ses_1ccabf5d9ffeZtpHMjPNmVB0Gb","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_d4FdF2L0rB7j1gZJE9naEtt7","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/AGENTS.md","offset":1,"limit":260},"output":"<path>/__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/AGENTS.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # MONDO Ontology Project Guide\n2: \n3: This includes instructions for editing the npso ontology. \n4: \n5: ## Project Layout\n6: - Main development file is `src/ontology/mondo-edit.obo`\n7: - individual terms checked out in `terms`\n8: \n9: ## Querying ontology\n10: \n11: - To look at a specific term if you know the ID:\n12:     - `obo-grep.pl --noheader -r 'id: MONDO:0004177' src/ontology/mondo-edit.obo`\n13: - All mentions of an ID\n14:     - `obo-grep.pl --noheader -r 'MONDO:0004177' src/ontology/mondo-edit.obo`\n15: - Regexes; all mentions of hand or foot:\n16:     - `obo-grep.pl --noheader -r '(hand|foot)' src/ontology/mondo-edit.obo`\n17: - Note that `obo-grep.pl` is in your PATH, no need to search for it    \n18: - Only search over `src/ontology/mondo-edit.obo`\n19: - DO NOT bother doing your own greps over the file, or looking for other files, unless otherwise asked, you will just waste time.\n20: - ONLY use the methods above for searching the ontology\n21: \n22: ## Before making edits\n23: - Read the request carefully and make a plan, especially if there is nuance\n24: - if a PMID is mentioned in the issue, ALWAYS try and read it\n25: - Use this command to fetch full text: `aurelian fulltext PMID:NNNNNN` (using the actual ID)\n26: - This also works for other URLs for scientific papers and for DOIs, if there are no access restrictions\n27: - ALWAYS check proposed parent terms for consistency\n28: \n29: ## Edits\n30: - IMPORTANT: Do not edit the edit file directly, it's large\n31: - Add edits should be made in the `terms/` folder\n32: - check out a term into `terms/`: `obo-checkout.pl src/ontology/mondo-edit.obo MONDO:1234567 [OTHER IDS]`\n33: - This will create a single stanza obo files `terms/npso_1234567.obo` which you can easily edit\n34:      - (note the colon is replaced with an underscore)\n35: - You can go ahead and edit the smallers files in the `terms/` folder\n36: - After edits, check back in: `obo-checkin.pl src/ontology/mondo-edit.obo MONDO:1234567 [OTHER IDS]`\n37: - if you like you can edit multiple terms in one batch, e.g. `terms/my_batch.obo`\n38:      - `obo-checkout.pl src/ontology/mondo-edit.obo terms/my_batch.obo`\n39: - checking in will update the edit file and remove the file from `terms/`\n40: - Commits are then made on src/ontology/mondo-edit.obo as appropriate\n41: - Note that `obo-checkin.pl` and `obo-checkin.pl` are in your PATH, no need to search for it    \n42: \n43: ## Specific Guidelines for MONDO Curation\n44: - When processing a request to add a more specific parent (is_a, subclass) to a term, do not remove existing parents unless _explicitly instructed_ to do so.\n45: - When removing a subclass (is_a) axiom, add a corresponding \"excludedSubClassOf\" annotation which includes the source of the removed axiom, and the ORCID of the curator, if available. Example:\n46: \n47: ```\n48: relationship: excluded_subClassOf MONDO:0002129 {source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432\"} ! bone cancer\n49: ```\n50: - Before finalising an edit for a session, we need to run `sh run.sh make NORM && mv NORM mondo-edit.obo` to normalise the serialisation.\n51: \n52: ## OBO Format Guidelines\n53: - Term ID format: MONDO:NNNNNNN (7-digit number)\n54: - Handling New Term Requests (NTRs):\n55:   - New terms start  MONDO:777xxxx\n56:   - Do do `grep id: MONDO:777 src/ontology/mondo-edit.obo` to check for clashes\n57: - Each term requires: id, name, namespace, definition with references\n58: - NEVER guess MONDO IDs, use search tools above to determine actual term\n59: - NEVER guess PMIDs for references, do a web search if needed\n60: - Use standard relationship types: is_a, part_of, has_part, etc.\n61: - Follow existing term patterns for consistency\n62: \n63: ## Publications\n64: - Run the command `aurelian fulltext <PMID:nnn>` to fetch full text for a publication. A doi or URL can also be used\n65: - You should cite publications appropriately, e.g. `def: \"....\" [PMID:nnnn, doi:mmmm]\n66: \n67: ## Syntax Checking\n68: \n69: - To validate syntax: `robot convert --catalog src/ontology/catalog-v001.xml -i src/ontology/mondo-edit.obo -f obo -o mondo-edit.TMP.obo`\n70: - Use `-vvv` for a full stack trace if there are errors.\n71: \n72: ## Mondo Guidelines\n73: \n74: ## Mappings\n75: \n76: Mappings are an integral part of Mondo. You should never create mappings unless requested by a user, if they do, make sure metadata is correct\n77: \n78: Mondo has an idiosyncratic way of adding metadata to mappings. Indicating the kind of mapping is important, this is dome by overloading\n79: the source qualifier and using an ID like MONDO:equivalentTo. Also the original source can be included:\n80: \n81: ```\n82: [Term]\n83: id: MONDO:0800447\n84: name: bleeding disorder, platelet-type, 13, susceptibility to\n85: subset: predisposition\n86: synonym: \"BDPLT13\" EXACT ABBREVIATION [MONDO:Lexical, OMIM:614009]\n87: synonym: \"bleeding disorder, platelet-type, 13, susceptibility to\" EXACT [MONDO:Lexical, OMIM:614009]\n88: synonym: \"bleeding disorder, susceptibility to, due to defective platelet thromboxane A2 receptor\" EXACT [OMIM:614009]\n89: synonym: \"susceptibility to platelet-type bleeding disorder 13\" EXACT []\n90: xref: MEDGEN:481244 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\n91: xref: OMIM:614009 {source=\"Orphanet:220443\", source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"Orphanet:220443/e\"}\n92: xref: UMLS:C3279614 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\", source=\"MEDGEN:481244\"}\n93: is_a: MONDO:0020573 {source=\"OMIM:614009\"} ! inherited disease susceptibility\n94: relationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/11608 {source=\"MONDO:mim2gene_medgen\"} ! TBXA2R\n95: relationship: predisposes_towards MONDO:0800446 {source=\"OMIM:614009\"} ! bleeding diathesis due to thromboxane synthesis deficiency\n96: property_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/bleeding_disorder_platelet_type_13\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\n97: property_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/6419\" xsd:string\n98: ```\n99: \n100: ## Obsoleting terms\n101: \n102: obsolete terms should have no logical axioms (is_a, relationship,\n103: intersection_of) on them. Obsolete terms may be replaced by a single\n104: term (so-called obsoletion with exact replacement), or by zero to many `consider` tags.\n105: \n106: ```\n107: [Term]\n108: id: MONDO:0100229\n109: name: obsolete Heimler syndrome\n110: def: \"OBSOLETE. A peroxisoome biogenesis disorder characterized by sensorineural hearing loss, enamel hypoplasia of the secondary dentition, nail abnormalities and occasional or late-onset retinal pigmentation abnormalities, in which the cause of the disease is a mutation in peroxisomal biogenesis factor 1 (PEX1) or peroxisomal biogenesis factor 6 (PEX6) genes.\" [MONDO:patterns/disease_series_by_gene, PMID:26387595]\n111: subset: ordo_disorder {source=\"Orphanet:3220\"}\n112: subset: ordo_malformation_syndrome {source=\"Orphanet:3220\"}\n113: synonym: \"bilateral sensorineural hearing loss, enamel hypoplasia and nail defects\" RELATED [GARD:0001687]\n114: synonym: \"deafness enamel hypoplasia nail defects\" RELATED [GARD:0001687]\n115: synonym: \"deafness-enamel hypoplasia-nail defects syndrome\" EXACT [MONDO:0009325]\n116: synonym: \"Heimler syndrome\" EXACT []\n117: synonym: \"sensorineural hearing loss, enamel hypoplasia, and nail abnormalities\" RELATED [GARD:0001687]\n118: xref: MESH:C535994 {source=\"MONDO:obsoleteEquivalent\", source=\"Orphanet:3220/e\", source=\"Orphanet:3220\"}\n119: xref: Orphanet:3220 {source=\"OMIM:234580\", source=\"MONDO:obsoleteEquivalent\"}\n120: xref: SCTID:721085000 {source=\"MONDO:obsoleteEquivalent\"}\n121: property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432\n122: property_value: IAO:0000231 OMO:0001000\n123: property_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/3222\" xsd:anyURI\n124: is_obsolete: true\n125: consider: MONDO:0100259\n126: ```\n127: \n128: Synonyms and xrefs can be migrated judiciously,\n129: \n130: We never do complete merges now, so there should be no `alt_ids` or\n131: disappearing stanzas. If a user asks for a merge, they usually mean\n132: obsoletion with direct replacement, as here:\n133: \n134: Example:\n135: \n136: ```\n137: [Term]\n138: id: MONDO:0100334\n139: name: obsolete viral infectious disease or sequela\n140: property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432\n141: property_value: IAO:0000231 MONDO:TermsMerged\n142: property_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/pull/3118#issuecomment-871858054\" xsd:anyURI\n143: is_obsolete: true\n144: replaced_by: MONDO:0100321\n145: ```\n146: \n147: No relationship should point to an obsolete term - when you obsolete a term, you may need to also rewire\n148: terms to \"skip\" the obsoleted term.\n149: \n150: ## Other metadata\n151: \n152: - Link back to the issue you are dealing with using the `term_tracker_item`\n153: - All terms should have definitions, with at least one definition xref, ideally a PMID\n154: \n155: \n156: You can sign NEW terms using with a tag-value like this: (don't tag pre-existing terms)\n157: \n158: ```\n159: property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator doi:10.1186/s13326-024-00320-3\n160: ```\n161: \n162: You don't need to add a date, this will be handled for you\n163: \n164: ## Relationships\n165: \n166: All terms should have at least one `is_a` (this can be implicit by a logical definition, see below).\n167: \n168: Some other terms may have relationships but these will generally follow existing patterns.\n169: \n170: ## Logical definitions\n171: \n172: These should follow genus-differentia form, and the text definition should mirror the logical definition. Example:\n173: \n174: ```\n175: [Term]\n176: id: MONDO:0000715\n177: name: lymph node adenoid cystic carcinoma\n178: def: \"A adenoid cystic carcinoma that involves the lymph node.\" [MONDO:patterns/location]\n179: subset: gard_rare {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\n180: subset: rare\n181: synonym: \"lymph node adenoid cystic cancer\" RELATED []\n182: synonym: \"lymph node adenoid cystic carcinoma\" EXACT [DOID:0060219, MONDO:patterns/location]\n183: xref: DOID:0060219 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\n184: is_a: MONDO:0001082 {source=\"DOID:0060219\", source=\"MONDO:Entailed\", source=\"MONDO:Redundant\"} ! lymph node cancer\n185: intersection_of: MONDO:0004971 ! adenoid cystic carcinoma\n186: intersection_of: disease_has_location UBERON:0000029 ! lymph node\n187: property_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/lymph_node_adenoid_cystic_carcinoma\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\n188: ```\n189: \n190: The reasoner can find the most specific `is_a`, so it's OK to leave this off, unless there is provenance to be added.\n191: \n192: ## Design patterns\n193: \n194: Check:\n195: \n196: `src/patterns/dosdp-patterns/*yaml`\n197: \n198: For the DOSDP design pattern which guides how the term should be created.\n199: \n200: ## 1. Gene-Related Disease Naming Conventions\n201: \n202: The documentation should include explicit naming patterns for gene-related diseases:\n203: \n204: ```markdown\n205: ## Gene-Disease Naming Conventions\n206: \n207: For monogenic diseases, MONDO follows the pattern: `{GENE}-related {disease description}`\n208: \n209: Examples:\n210: - ALG8-related autosomal dominant polycystic kidney and/or liver disease\n211: - MYCBP2-related developmental delay with corpus callosum defects\n212: - TUBB4B-related ciliopathy\n213: \n214: This pattern should be used even when users request alternative formats like \"disease - GENE\" format.\n215: ```\n216: \n217: ## 2. Synonym Attribution and Citation Requirements\n218: \n219: The current documentation lacks specific guidance on synonym citations:\n220: \n221: ```markdown\n222: ## Synonym Citation Requirements\n223: \n224: ALL synonyms must include proper citations:\n225: \n226: **Correct examples:**\n227: ```\n228: synonym: \"EBV-associated lymphoproliferative disorder\" EXACT [PMID:38882456]\n229: synonym: \"MDCD\" EXACT ABBREVIATION [PMID:36200388]\n230: synonym: \"CHD4-related neurodevelopmental disorder\" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163, Orphanet:653712]\n231: ```\n232: \n233: **Never use empty brackets:**\n234: ```\n235: synonym: \"term name\" EXACT []  # INCORRECT\n236: ```\n237: \n238: ### ClinGen Label Handling\n239: When ClinGen provides preferred labels, use the \"preferred label by community\" qualifier:\n240: ```\n241: synonym: \"Hajdu-Cheney syndrome-NOTCH2\" EXACT [] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\n242: ```\n243: ```\n244: \n245: ## 3. Design Pattern Recognition and Application\n246: \n247: ```markdown\n248: ## Design Pattern Compliance\n249: \n250: Before creating new terms, ALWAYS check for applicable design patterns:\n251: \n252: 1. Search `src/patterns/dosdp-patterns/*.yaml` for relevant patterns\n253: 2. Common patterns include:\n254:    - `disease_series_by_gene.yaml` - for diseases caused by mutations in specific genes\n255:    - `susceptibility_by_gene.yaml` - for genetic susceptibility factors\n256:    - `childhood.yaml` - for childhood-onset conditions\n257: \n258: ### Gene-Based Disease Pattern Requirements\n259: \n260: When following the disease_series_by_gene pattern:\n\n(Showing lines 1-260 of 432. Use offset=261 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# MONDO Ontology Project Guide\n\nThis includes instructions for editing the npso ontology. \n\n## Project Layout\n- Main development file is `src/ontology/mondo-edit.obo`\n- individual terms checked out in `terms`\n\n## Querying ontology\n\n- To look at a specific term if you know the ID:\n    - `obo-grep.pl --noheader -r 'id: MONDO:0004177' src/ontology/mondo-edit.obo`\n- All mentions of an ID\n    - `obo-grep.pl --noheader -r 'MONDO:0004177' src/ontology/mondo-edit.obo`\n- Regexes; all mentions of hand or foot:\n    - `obo-grep.pl --noheader -r '(hand|foot)' src/ontology/mondo-edit.obo`\n- Note that `obo-grep.pl` is in your PATH, no need to search for it    \n- Only search over `src/ontology/mondo-edit.obo`\n- DO NOT bother doing your own greps over the file, or looking for other files, unless otherwise asked, you will just waste time.\n- ONLY use the methods above for searching the ontology","truncated":true,"loaded":[]},"title":"AGENTS.md","time":{"start":1778977612889,"end":1778977612909}},"id":"prt_e33542453001WPks6W2F6Tr9ro","sessionID":"ses_1ccabf5d9ffeZtpHMjPNmVB0Gb","messageID":"msg_e33540b3f001ZbrpR16psUp6lD"}}
