ecular subtype by absent TP53 mutations and MYC amplifications that may be present.\" [DOID:0080707]\nsubset: doid {source=\"DOID:0080707\"}\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0026770\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: ncit {source=\"NCIT:C129445\"}\nsubset: rare\nxref: DOID:0080707 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: GARD:0026770 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nxref: MEDGEN:1389944 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: NCIT:C129445 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\"}\nxref: UMLS:C4330665 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\", source=\"MEDGEN:1389944\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0850198 {source=\"DOID:0080707\"} ! medulloblastoma non-WNT/non-SHH\nproperty_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/medulloblastoma_non_wnt_non_shh_group_3\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8567\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0956967\nname: medulloblastoma non-WNT/non-SHH group 4\ndef: \"A medulloblastoma non-WNT/non-SHH that is characterized as a molecular subtype by the absence of MYC amplifications and TP53 mutations, while chromosome 17 abnormalities may be present.\" [DOID:0080708]\nsubset: doid {source=\"DOID:0080708\"}\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0026771\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: ncit {source=\"NCIT:C129446\"}\nsubset: rare\nxref: DOID:0080708 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: GARD:0026771 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nxref: MEDGEN:1377534 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: NCIT:C129446 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\"}\nxref: UMLS:C4330666 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\", source=\"MEDGEN:1377534\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0850198 {source=\"DOID:0080708\"} ! medulloblastoma non-WNT/non-SHH\nproperty_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/medulloblastoma_non_wnt_non_shh_group_4\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8567\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1010151\nname: gallbladder disease 4\ndef: \"An inherited susceptibility or predisposition to developing hereditary gallbladder disease in which the cause of the disease is a variation in the ABCG8 gene.\" [MONDO:patterns/disease_series_by_gene, MONDO:patterns/inherited_susceptibility]\nsubset: omim {source=\"OMIM:611465\"}\nsubset: omim_susceptibility {source=\"OMIM:611465\"}\nsynonym: \"gallbladder disease 4\" EXACT [MONDO:Lexical, OMIM:611465]\nsynonym: \"gallbladder disease type 4\" EXACT [MONDO:RULE_1]\nsynonym: \"gallstones\" BROAD []\nsynonym: \"GBD4\" EXACT ABBREVIATION [MONDO:Lexical, OMIM:611465]\nxref: MEDGEN:370601 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: OMIM:611465 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"EFO:0004799\"}\nxref: UMLS:C1969115 {source=\"MEDGEN:370601\", source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0020573 {source=\"OMIM:611465\"} ! inherited disease susceptibility\nintersection_of: MONDO:0020573 ! inherited disease susceptibility\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/13887 ! ABCG8\nintersection_of: predisposes_towards MONDO:0700225 ! hereditary gallbladder disorder\nrelationship: excluded_subClassOf MONDO:0003847 {source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432\"} ! hereditary disease\nrelationship: excluded_subClassOf MONDO:0005281 {source=\"DC-OMIM:611465\", source=\"DOID:10211\", source=\"MONDO:Redundant\", source=\"NCIT:C122822/inferred\", source=\"OMIM:611465\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432\"} ! gallbladder disorder\nrelationship: excluded_subClassOf MONDO:0006026 {source=\"EFO:0004799\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0009-0001-6494-4831\"} ! urinary bladder disorder\nrelationship: excluded_subClassOf MONDO:0700225 {source=\"OMIM:611465\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432\"} ! hereditary gallbladder disorder\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/13887 {source=\"OMIM:611465\"} ! ABCG8\nproperty_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/gallbladder_disease_4\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8630\" xsd:anyURI\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9097\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1011033\nname: coat color dilution, MLPH-related, dog\ndef: \"Hereditary predisposition to color dilution alopecia in dogs due to a variation in the MLPH gene.\" [PMID:34751460]\nxref: OMIA:000031-9615 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nis_a: MONDO:1011321 {source=\"OMIA:000031-9615\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\"} ! hereditary disease, non-human animal\nis_a: MONDO:1011328 {source=\"OMIA:000031-9615\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\"} ! integumentary system disorder, non-human animal\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/ncbigene/607077 {source=\"OMIA:000031-9615\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\"} ! MLPH\nrelationship: in_taxon NCBITaxon:9615 {source=\"OMIA:000031-9615\"} ! Canis lupus familiaris\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/7271\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1030005\nname: mosaic SMO syndrome\ndef: \"A somatic mosaic condition caused by a postzygotic mutation (c.1234 C>T p.Leu412Phe) in the SMO gene. Two overlapping clinical syndromes associated with this variant in SMO have been reported; Curry-Jones Syndrome (MIM:601707) and Happle-Tinschert Syndrome. The syndrome is characterized by cutaneous and skeletal manifestations such as linear hypo‐ or hyperpigmented lesions, basaloid follicular hamartomas, palmoplantar pitting, atrophoderma, hypertrichosis, polydactyly or syndactyly, rib anomalies (rudimentary ribs), and limb‐length anomalies. Craniofacial and dental abnormalities such as dysmorphic facies, macrocephaly, craniosynostosis, jaw tumors (ameloblastoma) have also been reported. Additional abnormalities impacting the gastrointestinal, cerebral, ophthalmic, and gonadal organs should also be considered. Some of these features include anal anomaly, colonic adenocarcinoma, severe constipation, myelofibrosis and smooth muscle hamartomas, malrotation, medulloblastoma, cerebral malformations, developmental delay, cataract, microphthalmia, coloboma, glaucoma, and cryptorchidism.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40059/, PMID:27236920, PMID:30497210, PMID:31120550, PMID:32413283, PMID:7606318]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0027231\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nxref: GARD:0027231 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0015160 {source=\"PMID:31120550\"} ! multiple congenital anomalies/dysmorphic syndrome-variable intellectual disability syndrome\nrelationship: RO:0004004 http://identifiers.org/hgnc/11119 {source=\"PMID:31120550\", source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40059/\"} ! has material basis in somatic mutation in SMO\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3458-4839\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/7768\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1030016\nname: 22q-related schwannomatosis\ndef: \"A schwannomatosis that causes a predisposition to develop multiple schwannoma. It is diagnosed when an individual does not meet criteria for NF2-related schwannomatosis, SMARCB1-related schwannomatosis, or LTZR1-related schwannomatosis and both of the following molecular features exist: a loss of heterozygosity (LOH) of the same chromosome 22q markers in two anatomically distinct tumors or hybrid nerve sheath tumors and a different NF2 pathogenic variant in each tumor which cannot be detected in unaffected tissue.\" [PMID:35674741]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0028140\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nxref: GARD:0028140 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0008075 {source=\"PMID:35674741\"} ! schwannomatosis\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3458-4839\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/7663\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1040030\nname: GBA1-related Parkinson disease, susceptibility\ndef: \"A susceptibility or predisposition to Parkinsons disease in which the cause of the disease is the presence of a monoallelic pathogenic variant or risk allele in the GBA1 gene.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3254-7564, https://search.clinicalgenome.org/CCID\\:004931, PMID:19433656, PMID:19846850, PMID:19858467]\nis_a: MONDO:0020573 {source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0587-4693\"} ! inherited disease susceptibility\nintersection_of: MONDO:0020573 {source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0587-4693\"} ! inherited disease susceptibility\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/4177 {source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0587-4693\"} ! GBA1\nintersection_of: predisposes_towards MONDO:0005180 {source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0587-4693\"} ! Parkinson disease\nrelationship: has_characteristic MONDO:0021152 {source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0587-4693\"} ! inherited\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date \"2024-07-02T11:34:09Z\" xsd:dateTime\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0587-4693\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/7859\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060111\nname: SAMD9L-related spectrum and myeloid neoplasm risk\ndef: \"A susceptibility or predisposition to myeloid neoplasms in which the cause of the disease is a mutation in the SAMD9L gene. This condition is characterized by variable presentations of ataxia and cytopenia, myelodysplastic syndrome, monosomy 7 (acute myelogenous leukemia), and bone marrow failure.\" [MONDO:patterns/susceptibility_by_gene, PMID:29535429]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0028150\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"SAMD9L-related spectrum and myeloid neoplasm risk\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/, https://orcid.org/0009-0004-3069-7846] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nxref: GARD:0028150 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0020573 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/\"} ! inherited disease susceptibility\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/1349 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/\"} ! SAMD9L\nrelationship: predisposes_towards MONDO:0008038 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/\"} ! ataxia-pancytopenia syndrome\nrelationship: predisposes_towards MONDO:0018881 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/\"} ! myelodysplastic syndrome\nrelationship: predisposes_towards MONDO:0044645 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/\"} ! familial monosomy 7 syndrome\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8947\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060169\nname: HAVCR2-related cancer predisposition\ndef: \"Hereditary cancer predisposition due to variation(s) in the HAVCR2 gene, which confers the predisposition to susceptibility to subcutaneous panniculitis-like T-cell lymphoma (SPTCL) and hemophagocytic lymphohistiocytosis (HLH). Affected individuals typically present with multiple subcutaneous nodules and systemic B symptoms.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0028172\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"HAVCR2-related SPTCL and/or HLH predisposition\" EXACT ABBREVIATION [https://clinicalgenom