{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778977714609,"sessionID":"ses_1ccabf5d9ffeZtpHMjPNmVB0Gb","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_NTM15mEJzbqpQRSdun6tVCbW","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/docs/editors-guide/NORM.md","offset":1,"limit":120},"output":"<path>/__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/docs/editors-guide/NORM.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ## Check for and Merge Duplicate annotations in Mondo\n2: \n3: ### Description\n4: This command will check for and fix duplicate annotations, such as duplicate \n5: is_a assertions (parents), duplicate synonyms, and duplicate xrefs.\n6: \n7: ### Instructions\n8: \n9: 1. Navigate to src/ontology\n10: 1. Create a branch\n11: 1. In Terminal run :\n12: 1. `sh run.sh make NORM`\n13: 1. `mv NORM mondo-edit.obo`\n14: 1. Check the diff in GitHub Desktop. If everything looks okay, commit and \n15: create a Pull Request.\n16: 1. For example, see [https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/pull/3802](https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/pull/3802)\n\n(End of file - total 16 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"## Check for and Merge Duplicate annotations in Mondo\n\n### Description\nThis command will check for and fix duplicate annotations, such as duplicate \nis_a assertions (parents), duplicate synonyms, and duplicate xrefs.\n\n### Instructions\n\n1. Navigate to src/ontology\n1. Create a branch\n1. In Terminal run :\n1. `sh run.sh make NORM`\n1. `mv NORM mondo-edit.obo`\n1. Check the diff in GitHub Desktop. If everything looks okay, commit and \ncreate a Pull Request.\n1. For example, see [https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/pull/3802](https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/pull/3802)","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"docs/editors-guide/NORM.md","time":{"start":1778977714600,"end":1778977714608}},"id":"prt_e3355b1a2001VZwWIgxmTpH1nC","sessionID":"ses_1ccabf5d9ffeZtpHMjPNmVB0Gb","messageID":"msg_e335593