{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778977872231,"sessionID":"ses_1ccabf5d9ffeZtpHMjPNmVB0Gb","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_6iCTkuBdPdKyW6slCiddRuqT","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n+Implemented in PR #<NN>.\n+\n+Added a new MONDO term, `MONDO:7770000` `GPR161-related medulloblastoma predisposition`, as a hereditary neoplastic syndrome with `GPR161` germline mutation and `predisposes_towards` medulloblastoma axioms. The term is supported by `PMID:31609649` and uses the requested ClinGen affiliation source.\n*** Add File: /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/PR_COMMENTS.md\n+Added a new term for issue #9877:\n+\n+- `MONDO:7770000` `GPR161-related medulloblastoma predisposition`\n+\n+Rationale:\n+\n+- The issue requested a ClinGen priority label for a GPR161-associated medulloblastoma predisposition condition.\n+- Existing MONDO precedents for ClinGen cancer/tumor predisposition terms supported modeling this under `MONDO:0015356` `hereditary neoplastic syndrome` rather than as a generic inherited disease susceptibility term.\n+- `PMID:31609649` directly supports germline `GPR161` mutations as predisposing to pediatric medulloblastoma, especially infant-onset SHH medulloblastoma.\n+\n+What changed:\n+\n+- Added the new term with:\n+- textual definition citing `PMID:31609649`\n+- ClinGen-preferred exact synonym annotation using the supplied affiliation URL\n+- parentage to `MONDO:0015356` `hereditary neoplastic syndrome`\n+- logical axioms tying the term to `GPR161` (`HGNC:23694`) and `medulloblastoma` (`MONDO:0007959`)\n+- issue tracker link back to `https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9877`\n+\n+Validation performed:\n+\n+- Verified `GPR161` identifier as `HGNC:23694` using HGNC/NCBI gene resources.\n+- Verified literature support and contextual fit from `PMID:31609649` (`Germline GPR161 Mutations Predispose to Pediatric Medulloblastoma`).\n+- Ran `robot convert --catalog src/ontology/catalog-v001.xml -i src/ontology/mondo-edit.obo -f obo -o /tmp/opencode/mondo-edit.TMP.obo` successfully as a syntax check.\n+\n+Checklist completed:\n+\n+- [x] Read imported issue context\n+- [x] Reviewed existing MONDO precedents for susceptibility and hereditary neoplastic syndrome terms\n+- [x] Verified new external identifiers before use\n+- [x] Added the new MONDO term with definition, sources, and logical axioms\n+- [x] Checked syntax with `robot convert`\n+- [x] Committed only the ontology edit\n+\n+Environment note:\n+\n+- Docker was not available in this workspace, so `sh run.sh make NORM` could not be executed here. I used the direct `robot convert` syntax validation that was available locally.\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\nA PR_COMMENTS.md","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n===================================================================\n--- /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n+++ /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,3 @@\n+Implemented in PR #<NN>.\n+\n+Added a new MONDO term, `MONDO:7770000` `GPR161-related medulloblastoma predisposition`, as a hereditary neoplastic syndrome with `GPR161` germline mutation and `predisposes_towards` medulloblastoma axioms. The term is supported by `PMID:31609649` and uses the requested ClinGen affiliation source.\n\nIndex: /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/PR_COMMENTS.md\n===================================================================\n--- /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/PR_COMMENTS.md\n+++ /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/PR_COMMENTS.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@\n+Added a new term for issue #9877:\n+\n+- `MONDO:7770000` `GPR161-related medulloblastoma predisposition`\n+\n+Rationale:\n+\n+- The issue requested a Clin